# devlink-rescue classic: busybox init.
#
# ttyS0 belongs to the agent and nothing else writes to it: no getty, no
# kernel console. The agent's own log goes to /dev/console (the VGA screen),
# which is what the empty id field means, so whoever is at the machine can
# watch the session. respawn restarts it after @stop or a crash; @stop after
# a put of a new binary over /rescue/devlink-agent is how it is updated. A
# failed start (no ttyS0 on this machine) waits before the next try rather
# than filling the screen.

::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
# The tools: everything in /usr but busybox and musl is in this squashfs
# (board/classic/post-fakeroot.sh). If it fails to mount, the agent still
# starts, and the failure is on the screen and in dmesg.
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t squashfs -o loop,ro /rescue/usr.sqfs /usr
::sysinit:/bin/mkdir -p /dev/pts /dev/shm /tmp /mnt
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devpts devpts /dev/pts
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /dev/shm
::sysinit:/bin/hostname -F /etc/hostname

# The TCP passphrase from the machine's own disk, before the agent starts
# (/rescue/find-key says what it reads and how to supply one instead), and the
# network, beside it.
::sysinit:/rescue/find-key
::once:/rescue/net-up

# Serial on ttyS0, and TCP on port 2098 when /rescue/DEVLINK.KEY exists.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c "/rescue/devlink-agent serve /dev/ttyS0 115200 || sleep 5"

# A root shell on the second virtual console (Alt-F2), for anyone at the
# keyboard. No login: this image has no secrets and no network.
tty2::respawn:-/bin/sh

# The power button (acpid, /etc/acpi/PWRF/00000080) and Ctrl-Alt-Del.
# acpid logs every event it has no handler for, such as the lid, so its log
# goes nowhere rather than onto the screen.
::respawn:/usr/sbin/acpid -f -l /dev/null
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
